<title>USA: General Binding completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>General Binding completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Binding Corp said Thursday it has completed a previously announced purchase of the assets and business of Quartet Manufacturing Co, a manufacturer and distributor of markerboards, bulletin boards and easels.</p>
<p>Skokie, Ill.-based Quartet had 1996 revenues of about $150 million.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the transaction, which was effective January 1, 1997, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>General Binding makes and distributes business machines for binding, laminating and printing.</p>
<p>Shares of General Binding were trading off 1/4 at 29.</p>
<p>		((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
